# Cursor Rules

## Commit Messages
- Always generate commit messages in English.
- When I click "Generate commit message", ensure the commit text is in English.
- Use imperative mood and be concise in the subject line (max 72 chars).
- Optionally include a short body explaining the what and why (not how).
- Avoid emojis unless explicitly requested.

### Examples
- chore: update docker-compose and gitignore for postgres
    - Change postgres volume mount path to match bitnami image structure
    - Update healthcheck to use correct environment variables
    - Add postgres_data directory to gitignore
    
- feat: add feedback system and analytics routes
    - refactor: migrate metrics to analytics and update database schema
    - style: clean up unused UI components and update dependencies
    - fix: adjust docker-compose and PostgreSQL configuration
    - chore: update package.json dependencies and remove unused files
- chore: update Docker Compose service names for nginx